# Godot
.godot/
*.translation
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg.secret

# Android — the Gradle build template under android/build/ is SOURCE, not output
# (doc 13 §9 item 4): it is where template patches would live and it pins the
# build system the APK is produced by. Only what Gradle and the Godot exporter
# generate inside it is ignored.
#
# Gradle's own working state:
android/build/.gradle/
android/build/build/
android/build/local.properties
# Written by the exporter on every export, from export_presets.cfg and the
# project's resources — never edited by hand:
android/build/src/main/assets/
android/build/src/debug/
android/build/src/release/
android/build/res/mipmap*/
android/build/res/drawable/
# "WARNING: THIS FILE WILL BE OVERWRITTEN AT BUILD TIME" — the exporter says so
# itself, in all 40-odd locale copies:
android/build/res/values*/godot_project_name_string.xml
# Verbatim engine payload unzipped from android_source.zip — 215 MB of
# godot-lib.template_*.aar, each single file well over GitHub's 100 MB limit,
# and reproducible from the installed export templates in one command:
#   tools/setup_android.sh          (or --install-android-build-template)
android/build/libs/
# The plugin AAR is built from the Kotlin sources next to it; committing it
# would let a stale binary outlive an edited source. tools/setup_android.sh
# builds it.
# android/plugins/slacum_native.aar — TRACKED since 2026-08-21: this 34 KB
# artifact is load-bearing (the exporter packages it verbatim) and ignoring
# it let every export from 08-19 to 08-21 silently ship a stale plugin with
# no launch_args (third Fold session's root cause). `tools/build_native_plugin.sh`
# regenerates it; `tests/test_release_plumbing.gd` pins the symbol.
android/plugins/slacum_native/build/
android/plugins/slacum_native/.gradle/
android/plugins/slacum_native/local.properties

*.apk
*.aab
*.idsig
*.keystore

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*~
*.tmp
__pycache__/

# Python generators (`tools/gen_*.py`) import each other, so running one leaves
# a bytecode cache beside them. The generators are source; the cache is not.
tools/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent worktrees and session-local state
.claude/
# The suite is not concurrency-safe across worktrees (one shared `user://`), so
# every run points XDG_DATA_HOME at a worktree-local directory. That directory
# is a scratch `user://`, never source.
.xdg*/
build/playtest/
# Store listing assets are GENERATED (tools/gen_store_assets.py) and are ~20 MB
# of PNG per run. The generator is deterministic, so the repo keeps the recipe
# and the Play Console keeps the pixels.
build/store/
# On-device benchmark artefacts (tools/bench_device.sh): logcat CSVs, framestats,
# meminfo, thermal traces. Measurements of one run on one phone, never source.
build/bench/

# Hand-made XDG isolation roots. `tests/run_tests.gd` moves `user://` to a
# per-process temp directory by itself now (report 98 RR-57), so these should not
# appear any more — the pattern stays because the old
# `XDG_DATA_HOME=$PWD/.xdg` invocation is still in agent muscle memory and a
# 40 MB save tree is not something to commit by accident.
.xdg/
.xdg-*/
